WEBVTT

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:20.780
Here comes Speed Racer, he's a demon on wheels.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:25.580
He's a demon and he's gonna be chasing after someone.

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:29.540
He's gaining on you.

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:40.550
He's busy revving up the powerful Mach 5, and when the odds are against him and they're dangerous work, you'll do it.

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:45.900
Make your life's eraser, and you'll see it through.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:52.350
Go speed racer, go speed racer, go speed racer, go.

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:59.700
He's open flying as he guns a car around the track, he's jamming down the pedal like he's never coming back.

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:01.760
Adventures waiting just a half.

00:01:03.292 --> 00:01:08.052
Go Speed Racer, Go Speed Racer, Go Speed Racer, Go!

00:01:23.996 --> 00:01:25.196
Pushing up ahead, Speed!

00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:25.720
Mm-hmm.

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:03.440
Oh!

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:33.460
Isn't that the masked racer's car being unloaded from the ship?

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:37.400
This means there'll be trouble in the race.

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:40.680
Every time that masked racer's been in a race, there've been crashes.

00:02:41.190 --> 00:02:42.270
So there may be some more today.

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:44.170
But that's really why I came.

00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:47.350
I heard that sometimes he causes the cars to crash.

00:02:47.610 --> 00:02:49.110
But nobody's been able to prove that.

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:51.390
Well, maybe this time we can catch him at it.

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:53.130
So let's keep a close look at him, hmm?

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:03.540
He looks mysterious in that mask and sort of handsome.

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:07.740
He drives faster in a rocket, and he won the Grand Prix at Le Mans four years in a row.

00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:10.320
He's won just about every race he's ever entered.

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:11.300
No kidding.

00:03:11.740 --> 00:03:15.860
He's raced against some of the top racers in the world, and he's beaten them just like that.

00:03:16.956 --> 00:03:18.956
I hope I get to see what he really looks like.

00:03:19.868 --> 00:03:23.348
Sorry, but nobody's ever seen him, and they don't know his name or where he's from.

00:03:27.612 --> 00:03:28.112
Razor?

00:03:28.764 --> 00:03:29.564
He's in the big race!

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:33.080
Do you think any of the cars will crash in the race today?

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:37.540
You won't tell us that, huh?

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:40.180
Oh, hold it, Mask Racer. Let me get another shot.

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:43.430
Hey, we've got questions.

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:46.500
Wow, he didn't give us very much information.

00:03:47.390 --> 00:03:47.810
One side.

00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:51.150
Mr. Mask Racer, my name is Wiley,

00:03:51.190 --> 00:03:53.350
and I'm on the committee of the Trans Country Race.

00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:56.140
I'd like to talk to you for a few minutes if you've got the time.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:19.870
What do you say? Mr. Racer, every penny of that can be yours.

00:04:21.370 --> 00:04:21.870
Goodbye, what?

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:29.710
My Alpha Team has got to win the Great Trans Country Race.

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:35.390
With the Master in the race, my team won't have a chance unless you let your son, Speed Racer, join my boys.

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:38.180
With him on our side, we'd be able to beat any other team.

00:04:43.070 --> 00:04:43.430
...smackers.

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:43.670
Huh?

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:50.460
Well, will you let Speed Race in the Alpha team for 2,000?

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:52.280
Huh?

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:54.100
What's funny, huh?

00:04:54.820 --> 00:04:55.540
Why are you laughing?

00:04:56.610 --> 00:04:57.650
What are you laughing about?

00:04:59.240 --> 00:04:59.900
What's funny?

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:05.360
I'm laughing because you're offering only a measly $2,000 to Mr. Racer, so Speed will race on your team.

00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:08.540
While I'll pay $3,000 for him to be on my team.

00:05:10.010 --> 00:05:13.070
Well, how about it, Mr. Racer? I'll pay $3,000.

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:16.010
And here it is.

00:05:16.810 --> 00:05:18.570
I'll even throw in an extra $0.50.

00:05:24.130 --> 00:05:25.350
Only $3,400.

00:05:27.730 --> 00:05:28.670
How about it, Mr. Racer?

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:32.800
Oh, boy, the price is getting better and better.

00:05:32.940 --> 00:05:34.060
I hope it keeps going up.

00:05:35.750 --> 00:05:38.110
I'm willing to make it $5,050.

00:05:39.630 --> 00:05:40.030
There.

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:43.600
See the limit. Keep holding up.

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:46.340
$10,000.

00:05:47.690 --> 00:05:48.270
Going up.

00:05:48.680 --> 00:05:50.000
$20,050.

00:05:50.520 --> 00:05:51.320
I'll top that.

00:05:51.540 --> 00:05:53.180
I'll make it $50,000, okay?

00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:57.460
The money will be on Iowa.

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:16.400
The racer has a very good chance of winning the trans-country race, hasn't he, Speed?

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:17.940
Uh-huh, I suppose so.

00:06:18.940 --> 00:06:20.260
But would he really win?

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:21.200
What are you hinting?

00:06:21.620 --> 00:06:23.280
What about you being in the race?

00:06:23.380 --> 00:06:23.700
Oh.

00:06:24.230 --> 00:06:25.510
Why not enter at Speed?

00:06:26.050 --> 00:06:28.730
I'm sure you're the only one who could beat the masked racer.

00:06:29.140 --> 00:06:29.820
Maybe I am.

00:06:30.030 --> 00:06:30.930
But maybe I'm not.

00:06:31.230 --> 00:06:33.150
Anyway, we'll never know because I'm not racing.

00:06:33.230 --> 00:06:34.150
Wouldn't you for me?

00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:34.410
Huh?

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:36.820
As a special favor for me?

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:39.220
Oh, but it'll make my father angry, Trixie.

00:06:39.550 --> 00:06:42.790
If I know him, he'll come down once he sees you're going to win.

00:06:45.370 --> 00:06:54.060
I just signed up with Mr. Fixer of the Alpha Racing Team.

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:56.980
We have more spirit and the fastest car, so how can we lose?

00:06:57.160 --> 00:06:58.480
We're going to beat the Mask Racer.

00:06:58.600 --> 00:06:59.760
We're going to win the big race.

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:03.960
Too bad your father didn't take all that money Mr. Fixer offered for you to join the Alpha Team.

00:07:04.180 --> 00:07:05.360
Well, I'll see you after I win.

00:07:05.500 --> 00:07:06.260
Good luck, Slick.

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:24.530
The famous trans-country auto race will be starting very soon.

00:07:24.890 --> 00:07:29.710
The race, one of the most grueling and dangerous in the world, will be run over a course of 300 miles.

00:07:30.320 --> 00:07:33.420
Participating will be some of the top champions in the sport of motor racing.

00:07:34.010 --> 00:07:36.650
Let me introduce a few of the most famous to our viewing audience.

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:40.300
Here is the top driver for the Alpha Team, Mr. Zoomer Slick.

00:07:40.790 --> 00:07:41.490
He's in it.

00:07:44.030 --> 00:07:47.540
This is Driver X, known throughout the world as the Masked Racer.

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:50.200
He has been known to bring bad luck to many races.

00:07:51.040 --> 00:07:55.560
He may be known to bring bad luck to races, but he's one of the best drivers I've ever seen.

00:07:56.010 --> 00:07:59.970
In addition to the Masked Racer, one of the top contenders at a last-minute entry is a new...

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:12.820
Outcomer, Speed Racer, raced in very few meets so far, will enter this race driving the Mach 5, a special racing car designed by his father, Pops Racer.

00:08:13.380 --> 00:08:16.980
The race is expected to be a close competition between Speed and the Masked Racer.

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:19.250
It's supposed to be in the race!

00:08:20.280 --> 00:08:21.220
Here we go again!

00:08:23.920 --> 00:08:28.220
Speed, I don't want you in that race! Under no circumstances are you to enter! Understand!

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:29.380
Now, dear!

00:08:30.350 --> 00:08:32.290
Here we go, Pops will change his mind.

00:08:32.470 --> 00:08:34.750
I'm only trying to do what's best for you, son.

00:08:35.250 --> 00:08:38.830
You don't have enough skill and experience yet to race against the masked racer.

00:08:39.060 --> 00:08:41.300
It requires the utmost technical skill.

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:46.000
Sharp and well-trained reflexes are necessary over every inch of that racing course.

00:08:46.180 --> 00:08:50.000
Let me tell you about your older brother, Rex, who left home many years ago.

00:08:50.540 --> 00:08:51.940
He and I had a bad argument.

00:08:52.590 --> 00:08:56.470
It all started when he was 18 years old, the same age you are now.

00:08:57.000 --> 00:08:59.180
He joined a race without asking my permission.

00:08:59.460 --> 00:08:59.980
And he...

00:11:00.060 --> 00:11:01.960
It looks great. He wasn't scratched.

00:11:02.440 --> 00:11:03.880
I'm glad you weren't hurt, my boy.

00:11:04.740 --> 00:11:06.180
I'm very sorry, Pops.

00:11:06.630 --> 00:11:08.550
A few yards further and I would have been the winner.

00:11:09.120 --> 00:11:11.940
I did such a great job of driving, I deserve to win the race.

00:11:12.120 --> 00:11:13.200
Don't try to tell me that.

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:17.180
You deserve to lose the race because your driving technique was very bad.

00:11:17.890 --> 00:11:18.730
What do you mean bad?

00:11:18.730 --> 00:11:21.030
I would have won if my car hadn't gone into a spin.

00:11:21.290 --> 00:11:22.210
I know that, Rex.

00:11:22.600 --> 00:11:24.620
But if you had more experience, that wouldn't have happened.

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:26.400
Listen, Pops, I'm already an expert.

00:11:26.600 --> 00:11:29.140
But my beautiful new car is all smashed up.

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:29.980
What about that, huh?

00:11:30.480 --> 00:11:33.160
I'm sorry, but it was just an accident. I didn't mean to do it.

00:11:33.300 --> 00:11:36.500
I don't want to find you behind the wheel of a car again, and that's final.

00:11:37.220 --> 00:11:40.860
Then I'll have to become a champion without you, so I'm leaving home. Goodbye, Pops.

00:11:41.430 --> 00:11:46.670
You'll never be a champion, Rex. Mark my words, without skill and experience, you'll never get anywhere in the world of racing.

00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:55.860
I saw your brother Rex again, and that's why I say you need experience.

00:11:56.200 --> 00:11:59.540
But, Pops, don't you know that Speed's the best racing car driver in the world?

00:12:00.410 --> 00:12:01.410
The one who trained him.

00:12:01.910 --> 00:12:03.680
Hmm, I didn't ask you, Sprital.

00:12:05.050 --> 00:12:07.470
Well, it's getting pretty late, and it's time for bed, boys.

00:12:07.670 --> 00:12:08.890
Good night, Sprital. Good night, Speed.

00:12:09.230 --> 00:12:10.720
Night, Pops.

00:12:19.240 --> 00:12:20.540
Home again, where you belong.

00:12:21.150 --> 00:12:23.290
Mom and Pops miss you. So do I.

00:12:23.810 --> 00:12:26.390
I wish you could be here when I race against a masked racer.

00:12:26.770 --> 00:12:29.660
But wherever you are, wish me luck and beat him.

00:12:35.690 --> 00:12:41.830
Meanwhile, in a secret hotel room, the secret head of the Alpha Team, Mr. Wiley, is holding a secret conference.

00:12:44.510 --> 00:12:49.210
I want my team to win the trans-country race, no matter what the price, you understand, Slick?

00:12:50.440 --> 00:12:56.350
You can count on me, Mr. Wiley. It doesn't matter to me who's in the race, the mask racer or speed racer. I'm gonna beat him.

00:12:56.570 --> 00:12:59.740
Smart boy, I've heard that the mask racer's pretty tricky.

00:13:00.120 --> 00:13:02.380
The matter of trick he pulls, I'll be pulling it first.

00:13:02.860 --> 00:13:03.900
Don't worry, I'll beat him.

00:13:05.580 --> 00:13:07.100
That's the dirty fighting spirit.

00:13:07.340 --> 00:13:09.780
But when I do win, I expect to be paid a lot of money.

00:13:09.920 --> 00:13:12.160
I promise, Slick, you'll get everything you deserve.

00:13:12.880 --> 00:13:16.220
Hey, Mr. Wiley, I just found out that the masked racer is staying at the hotel sleeping.

00:13:16.220 --> 00:13:17.660
He's making plans to beat us.

00:13:17.780 --> 00:13:18.040
So?

00:13:18.260 --> 00:13:20.080
So we better make some plans to beat him.

00:13:20.240 --> 00:13:20.840
Don't worry.

00:13:21.500 --> 00:13:25.020
When I'm out on that track in the middle of the race, I'll do my stuff and he won't know what hit him.

00:13:25.780 --> 00:13:26.620
Good luck, Slick.

00:13:32.780 --> 00:13:37.940
I'm driving by the mother, neck and neck in the mouth.

00:13:38.100 --> 00:13:59.370
Be afraid.

00:14:01.720 --> 00:14:03.080
Isn't your name Spritele?

00:14:03.160 --> 00:14:06.290
That's what it is, and I'm stronger than I look, so watch out!

00:14:06.450 --> 00:14:07.510
I will, Spritele.

00:14:07.850 --> 00:14:09.050
What you come here for?

00:14:09.230 --> 00:14:10.720
To ask you to do something for me.

00:14:10.940 --> 00:14:12.940
I want you to give this letter to your brother, Speed.

00:14:13.700 --> 00:14:15.730
Huh? To my brother?

00:14:15.910 --> 00:14:16.290
Mm-hmm.

00:14:17.490 --> 00:14:18.940
Why don't you get to him yourself?

00:14:19.200 --> 00:14:20.680
I don't want anybody to know about it.

00:14:20.860 --> 00:14:21.540
Please take it.

00:14:22.970 --> 00:14:25.680
Well, mailman...

00:14:25.680 --> 00:14:26.420
I'll give you some candy.

00:14:26.520 --> 00:14:27.060
I'll take it.

00:14:31.850 --> 00:14:33.170
Now, be a good boy, Sprintle.

00:14:39.550 --> 00:14:40.490
But he was lost.

00:14:40.820 --> 00:14:43.760
He was looking for a post office, and I told him which route to take.

00:14:43.920 --> 00:14:45.330
Oh, come back!

00:15:00.280 --> 00:15:03.160
Huh? The Masked Racer? Hmm.

00:15:03.420 --> 00:15:04.680
What does it say, Speed?

00:15:05.050 --> 00:15:07.090
It doesn't have anything to do with you, Spridal.

00:15:07.230 --> 00:15:09.310
It's private, and you mustn't tell anybody about it.

00:15:09.390 --> 00:15:09.910
Do you promise?

00:15:10.110 --> 00:15:10.430
Okay.

00:15:10.890 --> 00:15:21.740
I've got to be in that race.

00:15:22.100 --> 00:15:25.470
I've got to beat the Masked Racer, and I know I can do it.

00:15:26.190 --> 00:15:27.810
Pop says I need more experience.

00:15:29.020 --> 00:15:29.960
I'll go to the track now.

00:15:30.510 --> 00:15:31.350
I'll get experience.

00:17:35.790 --> 00:17:41.710
you what are you doing here speed practicing you must not be in the race i will be and

00:17:41.710 --> 00:17:42.870
i can beat you i'll prove it

00:18:34.800 --> 00:18:36.180
Thank you.

00:19:04.600 --> 00:19:08.720
is nearly down to zero as Speed and Racer X race blindly through the night.

00:19:09.150 --> 00:19:12.570
One wrong turn, and it will be the end for either of them.

00:21:24.090 --> 00:21:29.870
Now we're in the center of a low low pressure area which is bringing heavy rains and high wind and see the waves

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:35.050
30 feet high and the tide is still rising driving conditions are extremely hazardous stay off the

00:21:35.050 --> 00:21:35.530
roads tonight

00:22:30.120 --> 00:22:35.080
dangerous. Now speed barely manages to keep a Mach 5 from skidding into disaster.

